<h2>Where should the filter controls go on the activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only. Each one uses the event-type Select (All events + the 9 types). Final styling will use the guideline tokens.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A: Filter bar above the table</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p><strong>Account activity</strong></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.8em">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-end;margin:10px 0">
            <div><div class="label">Event type</div><input class="mock-input" value="Sign-in failed" readonly></div>
            <div><div class="label">Search device or location</div><input class="mock-input" placeholder="e.g. Firefox, Berlin" readonly></div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.8em">Showing 4 of 45 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>A. Filter bar</h3>
      <p>Labeled controls always visible between the intro and the table, with a count line. Simplest; works the same at 320px (controls stack).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B: Failed sign-ins shortcut + type Select</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p><strong>Account activity</strong></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.8em">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-end;margin:10px 0">
            <button class="mock-button">Show failed sign-ins</button>
            <div><div class="label">Event type</div><input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly></div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.8em">Showing 45 of 45 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>B. Shortcut + Select</h3>
      <p>Same bar, plus a one-click button for the case support tickets are about. The button just sets the Select to "Sign-in failed".</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C: Filters button opens a popover</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p><strong>Account activity</strong></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.8em">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:10px 0">
            <button class="mock-button">Filters</button>
            <span style="border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:12px;padding:2px 8px;font-size:0.8em">Sign-in failed &times;</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.8em">Showing 4 of 45 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>C. Popover + tags</h3>
      <p>Controls hidden behind a Filters button; active filters show as removable tags. Tidier, but one more click and more code (popover focus handling).</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
